---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Expanded Metal Mesh — Specs, Prices & Anping Factories" description="Expanded metal mesh for walkways, grating, filtration, and architectural use. Diamond and hexagonal patterns, materials, and direct factory sourcing from Anping, China.">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-8">
    <!-- Main Content -->
    <article class="flex-1 min-w-0 prose">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-theme-primary">Expanded Metal Mesh</h1>
      <p class="text-theme-secondary">Expanded metal is produced by slitting and stretching a solid metal sheet, creating a rigid, open mesh with no welds or joints. Anping factories supply it for walkway grating, platform flooring, machine guards, filters, and architectural façades.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Materials</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Common Grades</th><th>Thickness</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Low-carbon steel</td><td>Q235, A36</td><td>0.5–6.0mm</td><td>Walkways, grating, general use</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Galvanized steel</td><td>DX51D, SGCC</td><td>0.5–4.0mm</td><td>Outdoor, corrosion-resistant</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stainless steel</td><td>304, 316</td><td>0.5–3.0mm</td><td>Food, chemical, marine</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Aluminum</td><td>1060, 3003, 5052</td><td>0.5–4.0mm</td><td>Architectural, lightweight</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Copper / brass</td><td>C11000, H62</td><td>0.5–2.0mm</td><td>Decorative, EMI shielding</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Common specifications</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>SWD×LWD (mm)</th><th>Strand Width (mm)</th><th>Thickness (mm)</th><th>Application</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Diamond</td><td>10×25</td><td>1.0–1.5</td><td>0.5–1.0</td><td>Filter, screen</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diamond</td><td>20×50</td><td>1.5–2.5</td><td>1.0–2.0</td><td>Machine guard, shelf</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diamond</td><td>30×75</td><td>2.0–3.0</td><td>2.0–3.0</td><td>Walkway, platform</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diamond</td><td>50×100</td><td>3.0–5.0</td><td>3.0–5.0</td><td>Heavy grating, catwalk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hexagonal</td><td>15×40</td><td>1.0–2.0</td><td>0.5–1.5</td><td>Architectural, decorative</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Square</td><td>20×20</td><td>1.5–2.5</td><td>1.0–2.0</td><td>Partition, ceiling</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">SWD = short way of diamond, LWD = long way of diamond. <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent">Estimate weight →</a></p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">What to specify when ordering</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Material and grade (e.g., SS304, Q235, 3003 aluminum)</li>
        <li>SWD × LWD in mm (mesh opening dimensions)</li>
        <li>Strand width and sheet thickness</li>
        <li>Sheet size (standard: 1000×2000mm, 1220×2440mm, or custom)</li>
        <li>Surface finish: mill finish, galvanized, powder coated, anodized</li>
        <li>Quantity in m² or sheets</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Price reference</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Product</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Spec</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Price Range (USD/m²)</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">MOQ</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Lead Time</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Mild steel expanded</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">20×50mm, 1.5mm strand, 1.5mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$8–15/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">100 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">10–15 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Galvanized expanded</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">30×75mm, 2.5mm strand, 2.5mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$12–20/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">100 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">12–18 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Stainless steel expanded</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">20×50mm, 1.5mm strand, 1.5mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$25–45/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15–25 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Aluminum expanded</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15×40mm, 1.2mm strand, 1.0mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$18–35/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">100 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15–22 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Heavy-duty grating</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50×100mm, 4.0mm strand, 5.0mm thick</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$30–55/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50 m²</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">20–30 days</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-theme-muted mb-6">*Indicative 2025–2026 ranges. Actual pricing depends on material cost, sheet thickness, order volume, and surface finish. Always request formal quotes.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">FAQ</h2>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What does SWD and LWD mean in expanded metal?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">SWD = Short Way of Diamond, LWD = Long Way of Diamond. These are the center-to-center distances of the diamond-shaped opening. SWD is the shorter dimension, LWD the longer. Example: 30×75 means 30mm SWD, 75mm LWD.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Is expanded metal stronger than welded mesh?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes — expanded metal is made from a single sheet with no welds or joints, so it has uniform strength in all directions and won't unravel if cut. Welded mesh can fail at weld points under heavy load. For walkways and platforms, expanded metal is the safer choice.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Can expanded metal be used for anti-slip flooring?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes. Choose raised (standard) expanded metal, not flattened. The raised strands create natural grip. For extra safety, specify serrated or pressed-in nosing on stair treads. Heavier strand width and thicker sheet increase load capacity.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What's the difference between raised and flattened expanded metal?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Raised (standard) has strands at an angle, creating a 3D surface with better grip and rigidity. Flattened is passed through rollers to make it smooth and thin — better for filters, guards, and architectural panels where a flat surface is needed.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">How do I calculate open area percentage?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Open area ≈ (1 – strand width / SWD) × (1 – strand width / LWD) × 100%. Higher open area = better airflow and drainage but less strength. Standard expanded metal has 40–70% open area depending on pattern.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Can I get powder coated or anodized expanded metal?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes. Powder coating (any RAL color) adds corrosion protection and aesthetics for architectural use. Anodizing is available for aluminum expanded metal. Galvanizing is standard for steel outdoor use. Specify finish type and color code when ordering.</p>
      </details>

      <div class="not-prose mt-8 bg-theme-secondary text-white rounded-xl p-6">
        <p class="font-semibold text-lg">Get quotes from Anping expanded metal factories</p>
        <a href="/inquiry/" class="inline-block mt-3 accent-bg hover:accent-bg font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors">Send an inquiry →</a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Sidebar -->
    <aside class="lg:w-80 shrink-0">
      <div class="sticky top-24 space-y-6">
        <!-- Quick Tools -->
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-5">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-theme-accent tracking-widest mb-3">QUICK TOOLS</p>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Calculate & Convert</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>
              <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Weight Calculator
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/tools/container-loading-calculator/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> Container Loading Calc
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/tools/fob-price-calculator/" class="text-theme-secondary hover:text-theme-accent transition flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-theme-accent">→</span> FOB Price Calculator
